From 21e44408abe135ce24578ec8fefcd3f3b9c6891d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 13:39:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08531/11362] Flip think-mode default to ON for gemma-4-31B
 induction (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6198)

Operator directive, on the matched-budget offline A/B this project's
standing convention required before a live-path default flip
(experiment_6199_gemma_think_mode_ab.json, landed this session): 10/10
games induced on both arms, think mode engaged real reasoning 10/10 vs
0/10 for no_think, and think mode had a consistent edge on induction
quality (heldout_accuracy, goal_predicate_accuracy) -- never losing where
the arms differed. The narrower levelup_positive_recall metric was
inconclusive (7 of 10 games showed no signal either way), but the
operator's call is to ship on the evidence collected.

ARC_LIVE_GENERATOR_THINK_SCORED_DEFAULT and ARC_LIVE_GENERATOR_THINK_
DEFAULT: "0" -> "1". induce_think_on() itself is unchanged; only the
constant it falls back to when CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_THINK is unset changed.

Updates test_arc_induce_think_mode_20260807.py: 3 tests relied on "leave
the env var unset" to exercise the OFF-path request-construction logic,
which broke when unset now means ON. Renamed/re-asserted the
defaults-resolver test to match the new shipped default, and switched the
two OFF-path byte-identity tests to an explicit CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_THINK=0
override -- decoupling "which path does this test pin" from "what the
mutable default constant currently is", so a future default change
doesn't silently invalidate what these tests actually verify. All 9 pass.

7 results/*.json artifacts get a freshness_acknowledgements entry: every
one was generated under the OLD default (think off), so this flip
affects future induce() calls only and cannot alter any already-recorded
value.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
